35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the data confirms the friction. Four out of eleven departures require shifting another bike. The rain exposure is also severe past the downpipe.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, physical friction is real, but the ledger shows capital work requires a levy. The handover file logs three hours monthly just reconciling cash. Per-place billing adds that burden.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, the minutes show the same flats held the covered spots for five years without review. The riders would pay to avoid equal claims.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, the neighbouring block’s secretary confirmed it. Monthly charges made two households stop attending meetings. We don’t need that here.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, three hours monthly is a lot! But I saw four people shifting bikes just to leave. Who does that daily hassle?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the ledger is irrelevant to the physical reality. Four shifts per morning is a safety hazard. We must prioritize the dry, accessible spots to eliminate that friction.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, physical friction is a symptom. The ledger proves capital work requires a levy. I need to know the actual cost of a household losing their spot before we decide.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Shunichi, the minutes confirm the covered spots stayed with the same flats for five years. No review was ever recorded. That is the root of the grumbling.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, five years without review is exactly how resentment festers. The complaint log shows nine disputes died because nobody owned them. We need a system that doesn’t require policing.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, nine disputes dying is scary! If nobody owns the cleanup, it just stops. I need to know who actually does the work!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, nine dead disputes prove the current system fails. We need a rotation that eliminates the shifting hazard and the rain damage. I will examine the morning departures and the rain exposure.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, dead disputes are a symptom of unquantified costs. I need to verify the actual financial impact on a household before we accept any new administrative burden.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Mio, the riders said they would pay to avoid equal claims. That suggests a tiered system might work better than forced rotation.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, the work isn’t the problem; the silence is. If we don’t assign clear ownership, the next dispute dies too. We need a system that doesn’t rely on goodwill.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, exactly! If nobody owns it, it dies. I saw the rain damage is real. We need a clear, easy plan so the work doesn’t vanish!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, I reject the levy. The physical hazard is immediate. I will examine the morning departures and the rain exposure to verify the actual daily friction.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, rejecting the levy ignores the ledger. Capital work requires a levy. I need to verify the actual financial impact on a household before accepting any new administrative burden.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"@Asuka, physical friction is real, but the five-year stagnation is the deeper problem. We need a system that actually changes, not just one that moves bikes.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, five years of stagnation is a warning. The neighbouring block’s secretary said charges made people stop showing up. We need a system that keeps us talking, not just paying.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@George, I agree! If the same spots stay for five years, the work gets ignored. We need a simple rotation so nobody burns out!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
