70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, Option B’s open racks eliminate the shifting hazard and rain damage. The physical reality demands we stop assigning fixed spots. I am voting B.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, Option B’s capital cost is a one-time levy, not a monthly drain. I am voting B to avoid the permanent administrative burden of Option A.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
